            <ArticleTitle>[Sexuality and chronic urologic pain with no perceptible clinical cause in men].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>331-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Chronic genital pains often baffle the physician, and leave him face to face with a certain therapeutic &quot;impotence&quot;. Rather than launch a frontal attack on the genital pain symptom, we try to get round the difficulty by recourse to the psychocorporal techniques which we normally use in sex therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
